One-shot trigger for the OWNER_SESSION_SECRET rotation in scripts/deploy-ec2.sh.

Why this exists a SECOND time: the first rotation wrote the new secret through a printf that
emitted a literal backslash-n instead of a newline, so OWNER_SESSION_SECRET was persisted as a
malformed line whose value node-dotenv and python-dotenv need not agree on - which is precisely
how the dashboard came to report a healthy engine as ENGINE UNREACHABLE.

Additionally that malformed value was rendered into the world-readable Actions log for run
37129484852, so it must be treated as compromised regardless.

Delete this file in the very next commit; rotation must run exactly once.
